WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.844
(SINGING)

00:00:02.766 --> 00:00:04.150
[PLAYS NOTES ON VIOLIN]

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:04.997
 Yes!

00:00:04.997 --> 00:00:06.580
[MUSIC - MARIAH CAREY,
 "FANTASY"] Oh,

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.600
when you walk by every night--

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.910
I love creating music.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.149
Having melodies run through
me is an incredible feeling.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:20.170
I just hear what I
hear, and I sing it.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.510
In the beginning,
in my first album,

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.970
I didn't know that
I was producing.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.070
Mind you, like, I'm a
teenage girl at this point,

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.260
and I'm sitting there
with grown men going,

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.960
can you raise the strings here?

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.637
I want to do just an
acappella moment right here,

00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:36.220
and then we'll bring
the beat back in.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.600
That is production.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.020
There's power in that,
and nobody really

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.520
wanted me to feel powerful.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.448
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:45.448 --> 00:00:49.150
When we talk about the
power of your voice,

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:54.290
there can be power in anything
from a whisper to a scream,

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:54.790
literally.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:55.090
[MUSIC - MARIAH CAREY, BRANDY,
 "THE ROOF"]

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.282
It wasn't raining yet--

00:00:56.282 --> 00:00:56.782
--yet--

00:00:56.782 --> 00:00:58.120
--but it was definitely--

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.055
--but it was definitely--

00:01:00.055 --> 00:01:02.590
Then there's the power
of self-expression,

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.160
and I want to do
this because this is

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.930
what I'm feeling in my heart.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.290
You said (SINGING) ba,
da, da, da, da, bop.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:12.790
Yeah.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:15.555
[PLAYS SAME SEQUENCE ON VIOLIN]

00:01:15.555 --> 00:01:16.055
Yeah!

00:01:16.055 --> 00:01:17.530
[LAUGHS]

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.210
As a singer, as a
songwriter, I've

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:23.530
chosen to be very, very specific
and real about certain things.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.590
Keeping things general,
but still trying

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:31.180
to reveal a specific emotion
that I was feeling in

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.490
hopes that other people
could relate to it.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.320
That stuff really
matters to somebody

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.260
that listens to lyrics.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.810
Music saved my life
in many, many ways.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:47.140
If I can do the same for other
people, then that's everything.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.020
I'm Mariah Carey, and
this is MasterClass.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.870
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:57.298 --> 00:01:58.774
[KISS]

00:01:58.774 --> 00:02:00.742
[YAWN-HOWLS]

00:02:00.742 --> 00:02:08.440
[LAUGHS] Please tell
me you got that.

